WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.268
-We are hanging out with
the great Mark Hamill,

00:00:03.268 --> 00:00:04.270
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.337
That's the one and only.

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.874
Now, Mark you've played several

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:10.643
iconic characters
over the years.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.012
And we thought we'd put your
knowledge of your own characters

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:15.982
to the test in a new game called
"Know Your Role."

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.016
Here we go.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:23.022
-♪ "Know Your Role ♪

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:24.323
-Now, here's how it works.

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:26.993
I'm going to give you
an obscure fact

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.728
about a famous character
you have played,

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:29.996
and you have to tell me
if you think

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.997
that statement is true or false.

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:33.032
You ready?

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.800
-Oh, it's true or false,

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.303
which is much better odds
than multiple choice.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.939
So that's good.
-Yeah, exactly. Yeah.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.140
It's kind of multiple choice.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.808
It's 50/50 multiple --
Yeah, it's two.

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:43.842
Yeah. Alright, here we go.

00:00:43.842 --> 00:00:46.546
First up, Luke Skywalker.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.914
He, of course,
is the main character

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.481
in the original
"Star Wars" trilogy.

00:00:49.481 --> 00:00:51.651
But there might be some things
you don't know about him.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.887
Let's see if you know your role.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:56.522
In the original draft of
"Return of the Jedi,"

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.457
Luke was going to
turn evil at the end

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:02.495
and team up with Darth Vader
to take on the galaxy.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:05.064
-I pitched that to George,

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:08.000
because I thought that's the way
things were going in "Empire."

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.305
I got the gloved hand
and I was dressed all in black.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:15.107
But, actually, George said, "No.

00:01:15.107 --> 00:01:17.109
It's a fairy tale for children.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:20.079
Luke is --
You know, he's virtuous.

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.247
He's the good guy."

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.715
So that's false.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.016
-Yes! Wow. Interesting.
Alright, good.

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:25.285
[ Ding ]

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:28.621
I kind of was hoping that.
I was hoping for that.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.123
Luke Skywalker once
crashed into a planet

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:33.659
where he met Kermit the Frog.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:35.828
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:38.197
-Well, you know why
that's a question,

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.233
is because since Frank Oz was

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.568
operating and performing Yoda

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:46.505
and I had done "The Muppet Show"
a month before he started,

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:48.875
we got visits from
Miss Piggy and Kermit

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.877
on Dagobah, the swamp planet.

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:54.647
So there's photographs of
us with big stars,

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.815
like I say, Miss Piggy.

00:01:56.815 --> 00:02:01.554
But, actually, that's not true.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.556
-You're wrong.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:04.824
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.993
-Huh?
-It actually is true.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.628
You went on "The Muppet Show,"

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.930
and the plot was that
you crashed on his planet.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.498
-Oh!

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:15.435
-We have a photo of you
as Luke with Kermit the frog.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:17.369
-Wow!
-There you go, yeah.

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:20.372
Yeah. How dumb am I?

00:02:20.372 --> 00:02:23.309
Because in telling you that
that was a false statement,

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.277
I referenced
the very "Muppet Show"

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:26.346
that proved me wrong.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:28.414
-That made it true.
Exactly. Right.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.616
That's why the game's fun.
-Duh!

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.617
-Alright, good.
Alright, here we go.

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:35.121
"The Force Awakens"
almost opened with a scene of

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:38.624
Luke's severed hand
floating in space.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:42.261
-It was a severed hand

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:45.064
holding a lightsaber,
flying through space,

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.633
and when it hit
the stratosphere,

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:49.935
the flesh and the bone
burned off.

00:02:49.935 --> 00:02:54.106
And they followed the lightsaber
as it went into the ground.

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:56.409
And I thought -- And I saw --
I read the whole script

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.578
and I thought, "Well,
there's great symmetry here,

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:02.248
'cause I'm in the first shot
and I'm in the last shot."

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.582
-Yeah, as if to say
your hand counts.

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:05.851
-Nothing in between.

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:07.419
But that is true.

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:08.421
-That is correct.
[ Ding ]

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:09.588
That is true.

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:11.691
That would have been cool.
I love that idea.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.494
Alright, let's switch things up.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:18.398
You also played the Joker in
"Batman: The Animated Series."

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:20.433
But the Joker has
80 years of backstory.

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:22.335
Let's see how well
you know the Joker.

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:23.735
-Okay.

00:03:23.735 --> 00:03:29.908
-In an alternate reality,
the Joker is Batman's mother.

00:03:29.908 --> 00:03:35.481
-Wow. You know, that's --

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.217
You know, I haven't read
all the material,

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:43.122
but, I mean, in my experience,
my version of the Joker,

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.257
I don't remember that
ever being the case.

00:03:45.257 --> 00:03:48.127
Maybe they did that somewhere,
and I didn't read it.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.695
But I would say that's false.

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:51.564
[ Buzzer ]
-It is true.

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:52.698
-Oh, no.

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:55.968
-In some alternate reality,
the Joker was --

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.504
yeah, was Batman's mother.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:02.341
-Does it say where and when and
what you're talking about

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:03.575
or just...

00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:05.778
-No. No. It has nothing.
It just says nothing else.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.046
-No. Alright.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:10.316
So no backup, just trust you.
-Yeah, I just --

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.251
It says "Google it."

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:13.419
It says "Google it."
I don't know.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.821
There's a story line
in the comics

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:18.824
where a monkey briefly
becomes the Joker,

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:21.393
and his signature move
is making his opponents

00:04:21.393 --> 00:04:23.863
slip on a banana peel.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.264
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:29.569
Again, that sounds stupid.
Yeah, I'll just say it's true.

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:30.769
-You're wrong. It's false.
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:33.606
We made that up.
The monkey wasn't the Joker.

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.674
But the Joker
could be Batman's mother,

00:04:35.674 --> 00:04:36.809
but it's not a monkey.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:39.144
-I was going to say,
is that any crazier than

00:04:39.144 --> 00:04:40.813
him being Batman's mother.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:41.947
-Let's not be ridiculous.
-Good grief.

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:43.482
It would never be a monkey.
Here we go.

00:04:43.482 --> 00:04:45.385
Let's get to Skeletor.

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:49.021
You're playing the
He-Man villain Skeletor

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:50.055
in the new Netflix show

00:04:50.055 --> 00:04:52.291
"Masters of the Universe:
Revelation."

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:53.692
Let's see how
you know that role.

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:56.996
Your character, Skeletor, is
often depicted as evil,

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.732
but according to
a TV special in 1985,

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.769
he actually loves Christmas.

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:05.671
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:08.007
No, he's the evil
Lord of Destruction.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.641
No, he must hate Christmas.

00:05:09.641 --> 00:05:10.977
[ Buzzer ]
-He loves Christmas.

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:13.179
-Oh!
-He loves...

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.881
They did a special,
and, apparently, at the end,

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:16.148
he really -- he loved Christmas.

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:17.683
I don't know where --

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:19.818
Again, I don't have any other
facts except that you're wrong.

00:05:19.818 --> 00:05:21.153
That's all it says.

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:26.659
-Well, this quiz is going to get
me kicked off the show.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.728
-Never in your life.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:31.364
You're a legend, bud.
Finally, here we go.

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:35.535
Skeletor is He-Man's
estranged uncle.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.972
-False.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:43.175
[ Buzzer ]
-It is true.

00:05:43.175 --> 00:05:44.410
I didn't know that.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.512
I just found that
out today, Mark.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.381
I found that out today.
It's a weird thing.

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:50.283
You go, "What?!
That can't be real."

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:53.786
Skeletor is He-Man's
estranged uncle.

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:56.255
-And now I'm wishing
you asked these questions of

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:57.590
Mark Wahlberg.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.125
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.125 --> 00:06:02.894
He would have done better.
-No way.

00:06:02.894 --> 00:06:06.098
No one better than Mark Hamill.
That's Mark Hamill.

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:08.600
Watch "Masters of the Universe:
Revelation"

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.204
on Netflix, July 23rd.

